  "description": "R-SQL-1 SQL-B, SQL-REL: does the independently captured ADO surface (ADODB.Connection, Provider=Microsoft.ACE.OLEDB.12.0, Mode=adModeRead, Data Source set through Connection.Properties) give the same metadata and rows as DAO for the same SQL texts (an outer join with a WHERE on the inner side, a Currency/Decimal UNION, LIKE with % and with *)? Each text runs through Connection.Execute (Fields Name/Type/DefinedSize/Precision/NumericScale/Attributes, then rows to EOF, then Connection.Errors); after the connection closes, a DAO engine opens the same fixture copy read-only and runs the same texts through Database.OpenRecordset.",
